   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I see, thanks. The documentation is too specific since SE = TRUE would be required for all estimated models, not just the EM (previously the MHRM automatically computed the information matrix during the iteration cycles, but I&#39;ve since found this approach quite unstable so it&#39;s been disabled). I&#39;ll update the documents accordingly.<div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Jun 29, 2020 at 3:35 PM stain stanley &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mailtoy...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Initial mirt() use `MHRM` method,I don&#39;t know `SE=TRUE` should be passed.  <br></div><div>In help(Wald),<span style=\"color:rgb(255,255,255);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(30,30,30);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">Requires that the model information matrix be computed (including<span> </span></span><code style=\"background:none rgb(30,30,30);color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">SE = TRUE</code><span style=\"color:rgb(255,255,255);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(30,30,30);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\"><span> </span>when using the EM method).</span></div><br>On Tuesday, June 30, 2020 at 12:01:31 AM UTC+8, Phil Chalmers wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Pass SE=TRUE to your initial mirt() call.<div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thu, Jun 18, 2020 at 1:55 PM stain stanley &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">mailtoy...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mirt_model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;<br>f1=q10,q12,q22,q23<br>f2=q11,q20,q24,q26,q47,q49<br>f3=q19,q21,q25,q52,q50,q58<br>f4=q04,q17,q18,q45,q51,q59<br>f5=q05,q13,q14,q16,q44,q57,q02<br>f6=q06,q15,q34,q43,q46,q56<br>f7=q31,q33,q36,q38,q40,q55,q48<br>f8=q01,q08,q09,q29,q39,q41<br>f9=q07,q27,q32,q35,q53<br>f10=q28,q30,q37,q42,q54,q60<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>df_core_irt_gpcm</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mirt</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">df_core</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mirt_model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">itemtype </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;gpcm&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">method </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;MHRM&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dentype </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Gaussian&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">verbose</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">technical </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta_lim</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">6</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">6</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)))</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> wald</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">df_core_irt_gpcm</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Error</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">No</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> information matrix has been calculated </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> the model</span></div></code></div><div><br>Attached pls find the data.frame.  <br></div><div>Where is the problem?<br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;mirt-package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-p...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/mirt-package/11d733c3-88e4-4fde-974a-7f614deb6e60o%40googlegroups.com?utm